{"number":42582,"title":"[aws_db_instance] Can&#39;t migrate from plain `password` to `password_wo`","body":"### Terraform and AWS Provider Version

```console
Terraform v1.11.4
on darwin_arm64
```

### Affected Resource(s) or Data Source(s)

* `aws_db_instance`

### Expected Behavior

I&#39;m expecting that if I migrate from the `password` attribute of the **existing** `aws_db_instance`, the `password_wo` password will be used.

### Actual Behavior

I found that the actual password after applying is something like an empty string. Also, I can see this in the plan:
```
  ~ resource &#34;aws_db_instance&#34; &#34;rds_metabase&#34; {
        id                                    = &#34;some_id&#34;
      - password                              = (sensitive value) -&gt; null
      + password_wo_version                   = 1
        tags                                  = {
            &#34;Name&#34; = &#34;some_name&#34;
        }
        # (71 unchanged attributes hidden)
    }
```
So, looks like the `password_wo` is missing in the plan, and the empty old password is applied.

